From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:46:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Fix me_disable CFR default

The ME code reads "me_disable" with CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI) as fallback,
and DISABLE_ME_PCI defaults to y, so the MEI PCI interface is hidden
when no value is stored. The CFR object however defaults to 0
("Enabled"): the setup menu shows the opposite of what the firmware
does, and saving the menu with its defaults turns the interface on.

Use CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI) as the default, like other CFR objects that
follow a Kconfig option (e.g. serial_console). This also covers Wildcat
Point, which shares this header and the ME code.

TEST=Built google/mccloud with CFR. Checked the CFR data generated for
lenovo/w541: me_disable defaults to 1 ("Disabled").

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
index 83950ea8b..e574a2683 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ static const struct sm_object me_disable = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.opt_name	= "me_disable",
 	.ui_name	= "Intel Management Engine",
 	.ui_helptext	= "Enable or disable the PCI/HECI interface of the Intel Management Engine",
-	.default_value	= 0,
+	.default_value	= CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI),
 	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
 				{ "Disabled",	1	},
 				{ "Enabled",	0	},
-- 
